com.jsp.usermanagement
│
├── controller
├── service
├── service.impl (optional)
├── repository
├── entity
├── dto
├── security
├── exception
├── utility
└── config (optional but recommended)

1)Controller Layer:-
  used for--Handles HTTP requests,Exposes REST APIs,Calls service layer,Returns ResponseEntity
**Controller layer handles client requests and delegates business logic to service layer. It should not contain business logic.
**Never write database logic here.
2)Service Layer:-
  used for--Contains business logic,Coordinates between controller and repository,Handles validation logic,Handles validation logic
**Service layer contains core business logic and acts as a bridge between controller and repository.
3)Optional: service.impl:-
  used for--Some developers separate:UserService (interface),UserServiceImpl (implementation)
**reason-Loose coupling,Easy testing,Cleaner architecture
**Not mandatory, but shows good design practice
4)Repository Layer:-
  used for--Communicates with database,Extends JpaRepository,Performs CRUD operations
**Repository layer abstracts database access using Spring Data JPA.Spring automatically provides implementation.
5)Entity Layer:-
  used for--Maps Java classes to database tables,Uses @Entity,@Id,@Table
**Entity layer represents database tables and defines ORM mapping using JPA annotations.
6)DTO Layer:-
  used for--Transfer data between layers,Hide entity from API,Control request/response structure(LoginRequest,UserResponse...etc)
**UserResponse,Customize response,Better security,Cleaner API
**We use DTO to decouple internal entity structure from external API contract
7)Security Layer:-
  used for--This is the heart of JWT.SecurityConfig,JwtAuthenticationFilter,JwtService / JwtUtil,CustomUserDetailsService (includes these 4 in jwt)
**SecurityConfig for
Configures Spring Security
Disables CSRF
Sets session to STATELESS
Adds JWT filter**
****JwtAuthenticationFilter
Extracts token from header
Validates token
Sets authentication in SecurityContext***
***JwtUtil / JwtService
Generates token
Extracts username
Validates expiration
Signs token***
***CustomUserDetailsService
Loads user from DB
Implements UserDetailsService***

*****Security layer handles authentication and authorization using JWT and integrates with Spring Security filter chain.
8)Exception Layer:-
  used for--Handle application errors,Return structured error responses,Avoid exposing stack trace
  should contain--CustomException,GlobalExceptionHandler (@ControllerAdvice)
**use @ControllerAdvice for centralized exception handling
9)Utility Layer:-(optional)
  used for--Helper classes,Common reusable methods,Constants
10)Config Layer:- (Recommended)
  used for--CORS configuration,ModelMapper bean,PasswordEncoder bean

******Complete Flow in This Architecture*****

1)Client sends request
2)Controller receives it
3)Calls Service
4)Service calls Repository
5)Repository interacts with DB
6)Response returns back

***For secured APIs:****
Request hits JwtAuthenticationFilter
Token validated
SecurityContext updated
Controller executes

***Explaination:-project follows layered architecture. Controller handles HTTP requests,
Service contains business logic, Repository handles database operations, Entity maps database tables,
DTO is used for request/response transfer, Security layer manages JWT authentication,
and Exception layer handles centralized error handling.
